      "candidate": "**Repaired Scraper (Python)**\n\n```python\n# gpu-price-scraper.py\n# -------------------------------------------------\n# Scrapes a GPU product page and returns a plain\n# dictionary (the expected gpu-price-schema-v1 format).\n# -------------------------------------------------\nimport requests\nfrom lxml import html\nfrom typing import Dict\n\ndef scrape(url: str) -> Dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts product details from the given GPU page URL.\n\n    Returns:\n        Dict with keys: product_id, title, price, availability, rating, url\n    \"\"\"\n    resp = requests.get(url, timeout=10)\n    resp.raise_for_status()\n    tree = html.fromstring(resp.content)\n\n    # Helper to get first match or None\n    _text = lambda sel: tree.xpath(sel)[0].strip() if tree.xpath(sel) else None\n\n    # --- Extraction ---------------------------------\n    product_id = _text(\"//div[@class='product-id']/@data-id\")\n    title      = _text(\"//h1[@class='product-title']/text()\")\n    price_raw  = _text(\"//span[@class='price']/text()\")\n    avail_raw  = _text(\"//div[@id='availability']/text()\")\n    rating_raw = _text(\"//div[@class='rating']/@data-rating\")\n\n    # --- Data\u2011type conversion -----------------------\n    price = float(price_raw.replace(\"$\", \"\").replace(\",\", \"\")) if price_raw else None\n    rating = float(rating_raw) if rating_raw else None\n    availability = (\n        \"in_stock\" if avail_raw and \"in stock\" in avail_raw.lower()\n        else \"out_of_stock\"\n    )\n\n    # --- Return as plain dict (schema: gpu\u2011price\u2011schema\u2011v1) ---\n    return {\n        \"product_id\": product_id,\n        \"title\": title,\n        \"price\": price,\n        \"availability\": availability,\n        \"rating\": rating,\n        \"url\": url,\n    }\n```\n\n**What changed**\n\n- The function now **returns a plain Python dictionary** instead of a `mappingproxy` wrapped in a tuple.  \n- All extracted strings are cast to the correct numeric types (`float`) for `price` and `rating`, matching the schema requirements.  \n- The scraper no longer yields tuples; a single dictionary with all fields is returned, restoring the expected extraction behavior."
    },
